1️⃣9️⃣ Age Ratio After Years

Suppose:

Father = 40
Son = 10

Current ratio:

\[
40:10=4:1
\]

After 10 years:

Father:

\[
50
\]

Son:

\[
20
\]

New ratio:

\[
50:20
\]

\[
\boxed{5:2}
\]

🔥 Don't multiply the ratio when ages change. Add the years to the actual ages.


